{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1507340-neither-left-behind-nor-forgotten-what-do-you-want-from-kinship","id":1507340,"title":"Neither Left Behind Nor Forgotten-What Do You Want from Kinship?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-03T17:57:53-07:00","id":1507340,"title":"Neither Left Behind Nor Forgotten-What Do You Want from Kinship?","content":"Yeah, slot this in with the Dreaming thread I still need to get around to, but in some ways, I should probably knock out a thread on my thoughts on expanding Kinship given that's a lot more set. But anyways, Kinship is generally regarded as one of the better parts of Beast, where it's most arguable heart is thematically at and is generally mechanically well supported, but I think it'd be fair to suggest that there's way for the mechanics to be improved upon or otherwise expanded, so to kick some gears into motion, let's have it as a chat-<br /> <br /> What do you like about what Kinship already does, and what more do you think it could do or would like to see it explore?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-03T18:55:17-07:00","id":1507347,"title":"","content":"I honestly would change very little to be honest!<br /> with one exception:<br /> I'd say that (most) beasts knows Mommy Deareast didn't create every single scary supernatural thing ever,but they do think Mommy has such a deep connecttion to all scarry supernatural beings it doesn't matter she isn't literally the originator of signle supernatural being,she's still the thread that binds them all. Case in points, (most) Beasts know Uratha came from Mother Wolf and Father Moon but they still think that since Werewolves are Scary and Supernatural they have a Deep Soul Bond to the Dark Mother.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-03T19:44:04-07:00","id":1507355,"title":"","content":"I like Kinship's concept overall, it makes sense that a Temenos/Anima Mundi Astral Entity of &quot;Monster&quot; that has a connection to the greater symbol of &quot;monster&quot; also has a connection to things thought of as monsters. I do have some nitpicks of the mechanics though.<br /> <br /> Classifications: No complaints here. I speculate Demon's exclusion is due to the Astral not actually having the specifics of the Unchained at all. Maybe it's because the God Machine covered its tracks too well, and Demons are included for securities sake.<br /> <br /> Thicker than Water: I'm not a fan of Thicker than Water giving a good impression by default. It might be my dislike of auto-successes biasing me, but I feel that while the familiarity of Kinship may soothe things, nothing should be taken for granted when social maneuvering with other supernatural creatures. I can easily see say a vampire initially regarding a Beast as potential competition, rather than family, from the familiarity that would supposedly help smooth things over. I guess I'd have the first impression have a bonus or penalty based on context, and afterward have it as a smaller general bonus to impression. I do like the bit where it helps with feral monsters, that make sense to me.<br /> <br /> Family Resemblance:\u200b Mostly, I would just like a clarification that a Beast can't spot anyone unless they are specifically looking for supernatural qualities in people. The text (which I may be misreading) gives off the impression that they automatically can tell when someone is supernatural and then describe the roll as if it's an action they have to take instead.<br /> <br /> Mother's Kiss: It's fine, I guess? I would prefer for it to be limited to someone with the Family Ties condition. I honestly can't say why, it just makes more sense to me that way. That said, it would be cool to see this concept explored more, with Kinship merits giving it more specific benefits towards a certain type of supernatural creature or something.<br /> <br /> Passing Resemblance: One of my favorites, actually. I like that the Horror is mutable, and I like that a Beast that hangs out with Vampires starts acting and looking like a Vampire.<br /> <br /> Family Dinner: The one I expect to be the most controversial bits of Kinship. My feelings on it are mixed. I like the dichotomy of this being the best way of feeding at High Satiety, and still being useful at low Satiety, but I feel like it very easily can make normal feeding feel irrelevant, even when it's a big enough part of Beast it acts as a classification for them. I think this really needs to be more emphasized as something Beasts do, right there with Normal feeding, but lowered in effectiveness somehow. I don't know, maybe it should be a roll with a set number of times a Beast can benefit from it over a period. Definitely, an area to explore more.<br /> <br /> Family Ties: Ok, this might be weird, but I'd like to see either being able to give this or an equivalent to mortals. Just hear me out: A Beast has plenty of mechanics Tying them to their Legend, but very little tying them to their Life. A Beast may be a Monster, but they also are a little bit Human, and that side of their Family is important too. I wouldn't have this grant any power to the Beast or whatever, instead, it's a protective ward against any who would harm the weaker of their family. I'd also have it be completely separate from Cults, though one could mix both if they wanted.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-03T20:50:19-07:00","id":1507363,"title":"","content":"On a narrative level:<br /> <br /> I wouldn't mind something like how Lunars in Exalted 3e have lots of ways to get someone's heart-blood besides killing them that resonate with different themes (in that case, they're Attribute Exalted so they have an alternative for each Attribute.). Giving each Family (or Hunger) a unique way of establishing Kinship that biases them towards certain groups could give some interesting dynamics to thing. I could see going the other way where as a Beast's Legend grows, they discover ways to gain Kinship in ways that resonate with their Legend instead of something more splat-focused.<br /> <br /> On a mechanical level:<br /> <br /> I would love some ST-level advice on how far to take things like Kinship Merits. It doesn't have to have one set mode. A dial could be good too. But it can be hard for groups (esp. ones not super mechanically inclined or with deep knowledge of the other games) to know exactly what a Beast can learn from their bonds with other supernaturals. Can that directly copy splat-specific Merits or only get similar Merits that can overlap in function? Those sorts of questions don't necessarily have a single right answer, but it could use some guidelines since it's very &quot;whatever the ST feels&quot; at the moment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-03T20:50:47-07:00","id":1507364,"title":"","content":"Was gonna write something, but then I realized that I forgot most of Kinship mechanics, so, uh\u2026<br /> <br /> Oh, did we have anything that works alone in a Beast context, other than just crossover hooks? Something like how Hunter 2e looks less at the other gamelines for their hunts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":".  right - write 04-03-2023, 11:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-03T21:28:37-07:00","id":1507371,"title":"","content":"I've said it elsewhere, but the big one is this: now that the way the Dream works is pinned down a little more, the Begotten's internal mythological framework for why other monsters resonate with them shouldn't be that they came from the Primordial Dream, it should be that they came from the Mother's Land.<br /> <br /> The world-soul is sufficiently <i>terra incognita</i> that you can draw lines between the hungry cousins of the Children of the Dark Mother and the place she supposedly makes her Lair without having to speculate on why so few of them have any significant magical ties to human culture.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-03T21:43:14-07:00","id":1507372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1507340-neither-left-behind-nor-forgotten-what-do-you-want-from-kinship?p=1507364#post1507364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was gonna write something, but then I realized that I forgot most of Kinship mechanics, so, uh\u2026<br /> <br /> Oh, did we have anything that works alone in a Beast context, other than just crossover hooks? Something like how Hunter 2e looks less at the other gamelines for their hunts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some. In a Beast-only world, Beasts can tell others Beasts are Beasts. That\u2019s about it. Most of their stuff works with any supernatural creature, including spirits and ghosts. They can also figure out details on any supernatural creatures, not just the playable ones, and enjoy a sizable bonus for interacting with &quot;feral supernatural beings&quot;. Given that they do stuff in the Astral, you can have pretty much all of the Kinship stuff work just fine. Of course, the more weird stuff populates your world, the more opportunity for them to use the Kinship stuff.<br /> <br /> Edit: to phrase it another way, while the abilities do work for crossover, the only assumption made for them is that there are other supernatural creatures besides Beasts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 04-04-2023, 12:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-03T23:27:53-07:00","id":1507377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1507340-neither-left-behind-nor-forgotten-what-do-you-want-from-kinship?p=1507364#post1507364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was gonna write something, but then I realized that I forgot most of Kinship mechanics, so, uh\u2026<br /> <br /> Oh, did we have anything that works alone in a Beast context, other than just crossover hooks? Something like how Hunter 2e looks less at the other gamelines for their hunts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like I need to clarify on a point in the interest of the question: Beast (should) operate(s) on an assumption that there's at least always some other kind of monster at play in the world other than themselves, even if at a minimum you're talking Goetia, but more realistically at least Horrors from the Chronicles core Horror Creation System-The Beast can have Kinship and gain advantages from that Kinship (and offer advantages) with the Black-Eyed Kids as much as they can the Kindred. It does it pretty well so long as you have the tools to make your own monsters....with the obvious caveat that none of the Beast books have the Horror Creation System. This is an oversight that needs correction moving forward.<br /> <br /> As a basic rundown of my thoughts for Kinship (mostly as it exists now, not going into ideas for Beast, Family, or Human Kinship):<br /> <br /> 1*) Family Ties should be a scaleable tiered Condition from 1 to Five, for making more meaningful differences between relationships of varying depths.<br /> <br /> 1.5*) and honestly, a set of paired conditions representing each side of the Kinship, one for the Beast and one for the Kin, to better represent the way feelings can differ and grow and make it work to build up one side and another, and also build into point 2.<br /> <br /> 2) Attach different advantages that a Beast can get from a relationship to those different tiers to again incentivize building those relationships, and also emphasize the way sympathy is also &quot;contagious&quot; of each other's nature for people in relationships to Beasts.<br /> <br /> 2.5) In particular, it also means the Kin can gain more advantages and become more like the Beast, possibly by getting access to Birthrights, Normal Effects of an Atavism/Nightmare, provide alternate means of mitigating their own Integrity threats in a way that still inflicts a more monstrous nature on them (akin to Inuring spells or trading breaking points for Banes in Requiem, but unique in it's predication on the relationship to the Beast), and access to Kinship Merits from other associated monsters, because I think a vampire and a changeling who are Kin with a Beast but never meet each other should still have the chance to look more alike than not. Being Kin with a Beast should allow them warp and become weirder.<br /> <br /> 3) In the spirit of Kinship being the actual Integrity-alike of Beast in a sort of operational space shared with the Conviction and Loyalty Touchstones of Renegades, and in support of the idea that you are the company you keep, maybe an adjacent Condition set that reflects whether you don't really have connection, if the majority of your connections are trying to maintain their humanity, or if the majority of them don't give a shit, and a soft presence effect for it.<br /> <br /> *Yes, I'm ripping off Golden Sky Stories, why wouldn't I?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-04T12:50:17-07:00","id":1507433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1507340-neither-left-behind-nor-forgotten-what-do-you-want-from-kinship?p=1507377#post1507377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1*) Family Ties should be a scaleable tiered Condition from 1 to Five, for making more meaningful differences between relationships of varying depths.</div> </div> </div> </div> That\u2019s a great idea actually.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1507340-neither-left-behind-nor-forgotten-what-do-you-want-from-kinship?p=1507377#post1507377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1.5*) and honestly, a set of paired conditions representing each side of the Kinship, one for the Beast and one for the Kin, to better represent the way feelings can differ and grow and make it work to build up one side and another, and also build into point 2.</div> </div> </div> </div> Again, great idea. That\u2019s potentially a lot of conditions though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1507340-neither-left-behind-nor-forgotten-what-do-you-want-from-kinship?p=1507377#post1507377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> 2 Attach different advantages that a Beast can get from a relationship to those different tiers to again incentivize building those relationships, and also emphasize the way sympathy is also &quot;contagious&quot; of each other's nature for people in relationships to Beasts.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yep, make sense. Would these be different from the ones they already get for doing so, or would you prefer to make new benefits?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1507340-neither-left-behind-nor-forgotten-what-do-you-want-from-kinship?p=1507377#post1507377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> 2.5) In particular, it also means the Kin can gain more advantages and become more like the Beast, possibly by getting access to Birthrights, Normal Effects of an Atavism/Nightmare, provide alternate means of mitigating their own Integrity threats in a way that still inflicts a more monstrous nature on them (akin to Inuring spells or trading breaking points for Banes in Requiem, but unique in it's predication on the relationship to the Beast), and access to Kinship Merits from other associated monsters, because I think a vampire and a changeling who are Kin with a Beast but never meet each other should still have the chance to look more alike than not. Being Kin with a Beast should allow them warp and become weirder.</div> </div> </div> </div> definitely a fan, most relationships are\u2019t just one way, and with one gaining supernatural power from a relationship implies something similar should happen on the other end. This also goes more into helping people accept and embrace their own monstrosity. Maybe that gets them channeling their monstrosity into something positive, maybe it grants them enough power to go laughing past their own Integrity alike.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1507340-neither-left-behind-nor-forgotten-what-do-you-want-from-kinship?p=1507377#post1507377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> 3) In the spirit of Kinship being the actual Integrity-alike of Beast in a sort of operational space shared with the Conviction and Loyalty Touchstones of Renegades, and in support of the idea that you are the company you keep, maybe an adjacent Condition set that reflects whether you don't really have connection, if the majority of your connections are trying to maintain their humanity, or if the majority of them don't give a shit, and a soft presence effect for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this one too actually\u2026but I now have a growing concern. I believe everyone of these is a good idea, don\u2019t get me wrong. They all add needed Depth\u2026but Complexity too. I don\u2019t think your ratio of these concepts have too bad a ratio\u2026but their implementation might. I get that it\u2019s in many ways mirroring Satiety\u2019s effect on stuff, but I\u2019m worried a second tier system may be unwieldy for actual play. Maybe not, I\u2019m not a game designer, but I think it\u2019s something to keep in mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 04-05-2023, 05:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-04T17:29:48-07:00","id":1507442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1507340-neither-left-behind-nor-forgotten-what-do-you-want-from-kinship?p=1507433#post1507433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I like this one too actually\u2026but I now have a growing concern. I believe everyone of these is a good idea, don\u2019t get me wrong. They all add needed Depth\u2026but Complexity too. I don\u2019t think your ratio of these concepts have too bad a ratio\u2026but their implementation might. I get that it\u2019s in many ways mirroring Satiety\u2019s effect on stuff, but I\u2019m worried a second tier system may be unwieldy for actual play. Maybe not, I\u2019m not a game designer, but I think it\u2019s something to keep in mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a definite concern, but an overfleshed concept can always be condensed and chopped at.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-04T18:44:21-07:00","id":1507448,"title":"","content":"Complexity is also something you can make optional. Down &amp; Dirty can exist next to full combat for groups to use as they like. You can have a simpler Kinship system for people that don't want it to be too big, or something more details for people like myself that are interested in doing more with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-04T18:58:01-07:00","id":1507450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1507340-neither-left-behind-nor-forgotten-what-do-you-want-from-kinship?p=1507448#post1507448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Complexity is also something you can make optional. Down &amp; Dirty can exist next to full combat for groups to use as they like. You can have a simpler Kinship system for people that don't want it to be too big, or something more details for people like myself that are interested in doing more with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Organizational rules are a good demonstration of this-a lot of what they do used to be covered by Status and a number of other merits, and those are still usable if you don't want to dive into the full Krewe/Cult/Conspiracy systems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-05T01:05:27-07:00","id":1507460,"title":"","content":"I gave your post a deserved upvote. It covers all fragmentary ideas I had to improve Kinship and goes well beyond them.<br /> <br /> I do want to tackle an unmentioned matter. Based on what I saw on the Forums, people seem to be warmly predisposed to the idea of Kinship with Mortals. The homebrew Obcasus Rite that allows that is massively liked. I also think that it's a conceptual gold mine for the game, even if Kinships to Mortals and Monsters don't get equal metaphysical power. They could organically connect Beasts to their Cultists and human family and friends, which would underscore the &quot;No Neat Boxes&quot; principle. It could evoke the subject of monstrosity within humanity and humanity within monstrosity.<br /> <br /> Even if by default Beasts consider Mortal Kinships impossible, there could be an in-universe way to bridge the gap, because having options is more fun than a hard &quot;no&quot; (the same could apply to the Unchained.). It could also be neat to consider if Kinships could be formed to the local vindictive tiger that villagers take pains not to upset, or the old catfish that snapped hundreds of fishing lines and swallowed dozens of pets whole. They're not monsters in the common understanding of the term, but they're the kinds of things that make their mark in the common consciousness.<br /> <br /> That would likely require ironing out what allows for Kinship. Can it only be formed to beings that the bulk of humanity would consider monsters? Only beings approved by the Dark Mother? Beings who cause Integrity loss, leaving their mark on he Primordial Dream? Whichever is most thematically appropriate, and allows for most versimilitude.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-05T02:33:55-07:00","id":1507465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1507340-neither-left-behind-nor-forgotten-what-do-you-want-from-kinship?p=1507460#post1507460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I gave your post a deserved upvote. It covers all fragmentary ideas I had to improve Kinship and goes well beyond them.<br /> <br /> I do want to tackle an unmentioned matter. Based on what I saw on the Forums, people seem to be warmly predisposed to the idea of Kinship with Mortals. The homebrew Obcasus Rite that allows that is massively liked. I also think that it's a conceptual gold mine for the game, even if Kinships to Mortals and Monsters don't get equal metaphysical power. They could organically connect Beasts to their Cultists and human family and friends, which would underscore the &quot;No Neat Boxes&quot; principle. It could evoke the subject of monstrosity within humanity and humanity within monstrosity.<br /> <br /> Even if by default Beasts consider Mortal Kinships impossible, there could be an in-universe way to bridge the gap, because having options is more fun than a hard &quot;no&quot; (the same could apply to the Unchained.). It could also be neat to consider if Kinships could be formed to the local vindictive tiger that villagers take pains not to upset, or the old catfish that snapped hundreds of fishing lines and swallowed dozens of pets whole. They're not monsters in the common understanding of the term, but they're the kinds of things that make their mark in the common consciousness.<br /> <br /> That would likely require ironing out what allows for Kinship. Can it only be formed to beings that the bulk of humanity would consider monsters? Only beings approved by the Dark Mother? Beings who cause Integrity loss, leaving their mark on he Primordial Dream? Whichever is most thematically appropriate, and allows for most versimilitude.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dig this. Maybe \u201cMother\u2019s Blood\u201d for the \u2018real\u2019 monsters, and \u201cMother\u2019s Breath\u201d for the \u2018If it quacks like a duck\u2026\u201d monsters?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-05T13:04:25-07:00","id":1507505,"title":"","content":"I'll try and get out thoughts on Human Kinship later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-13T18:07:42-07:00","id":1508311,"title":"","content":"So way back in the wayback machine (2019, it was 2019), when the madness overtook me, I went to Cinder and came up with a laundry list of priorities for what would actually need to be done with Beast. The first two were unanimous-Heroes, and then the Astral/Dreaming. I don't remember, and can't check right now, if Cinder agreed with me on the third, but for me, expanding Kinship was the next major thing-not that what we had wasn't good, but there was definitely more to do with it. My main thing was ripping off Golden Sky Stories' main advancement mechanic and making sure Kin got more out of the relationship (Not that it matters all that much for the Beast, the bigger thing for them) was having gradiated access their kinship benefits so they have more reason to invest into a relationship. But beyond that, I wanted to cover different layers of Kinship by adding the sub-categories of Beast Kinship, Family Kinship*, and Human Kinship.<br /> <br /> My main interest was that I was fascinated by the metaphysical position Beasts have as Temenotic Goetia** meaning that they were a multitudinous entity-or, more accurately, they were a part of a whole lot of other people who <i>had</i> those fears and hungers. That was a angle Beast never really tackled or took advantage. There were a lot of other benefits to Human Kinship, in theory-Beast could directly get into how all fiction has a level of psychological metaphor in it, it allowed us to more readily begin constructing Beast's unspoken notion that it's neck of the world has the internal worlds and external world is one as a more solid and open thing, and it allowed people to more readily understanding Beasts as psychological actors (if they chose to be) and how that ties into their role of mythmakers and legend-takers-but mostly it was a chance to get <i>weird</i> and I like <i>weird</i>.<br /> <br /> Of course, it had to be distinctive from other Kinship, and that became doubly true when I grokked onto Kinship being akin to Deviant's Touchstone &quot;Integrity&quot; System. That there was a power in not really being able to understand themselves by direct comparison to humanity but in how the monsters they related to related to humanity, and how that reflected back on that was a bonus way to think about it and cut a line between the two. Plus my argument about the interesting metaphysical difference has it's clear difference-Beasts are Astral Symbols of the idea of monster and feel kinship to those who arguably bear the same semiotic device, but with humans they get more into the meaning and reason behind the creation of those symbols in the first place.<br /> <br /> (I don't have any place to put this, so I'll just take this interrim to mention I don't think we need really do anything for understanding Kinship and what allows for it-Beasts have a different relationship with humanity than with monsters, and thus it follows, and what is and is not Kin is pretty clear cut, my main evidence for that being that most people were questioning if Deviants were Kin while my handful of remaining questions of what counts include those with the Cursed Merit and the question of if the Ascending Ones' alchemy actually counts.)<br /> <br /> I'll lay out the three particular ideas I had, but admittedly the big thing is that while the whole idea feels meaningful and weighty, that it has bearing that could be of real aid to Beast, it's hard to actually get down into what it should do.<br /> <br /> 1) Touchstone. Even with the comprehension about Kinship and it's Integrity role, pretty much everyone I know has said that some kind of Touchstone would be a good idea-and I agree, but I do't know <i>why,</i> mostly because I can't really fathom what it would <i>do</i>. Asides from laying a fat thumb of the scales for Idea 5 from normal Kinship in favor of being associated with human inclined entitites, I'm not quite sure what a Beast should get out of it, or what a touchstone might get in kind.<br /> <br /> 2) Knowing THose Like Unto the Beast. THis idea is basically letting Beasts know if someone around them would be in their own Family as Beast, if they would have the same Hunger as them if they were a Beast, or both, and perhaps getting to know the specifics at the cost of becoming a little too much like the person, possibly temporarily taking on Aspirations or what not. Issues of treading on Needs Must and how cheap this makes looking for a Satiation victim be asides (and those are already big issues), it's also....fuck, I knew there was an additional problem, but I can't think of it.<br /> <br /> 3) <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1386002-harmony-from-the-din-lair-goetic-metaphysics-and-categorical-imperatives#post1386002\">Basically the Lore System</a>. I wanted to give a hook where Beasts could tempt them to their more assertive sides, (even monstrous sides) by offering up their benefits to someone who decided to break societal taboos (Or, hell, just needs the chance to meaningfully step out of their shell) to get what they wanted, allowing them to act just a little more Beastly-and of course, the ability to have it bite them in the ass.<br /> <br /> Over time, I've become dissatisfied with those ideas, but I still <i>feel</i> like Human Kinship is something that should be done, sooooooo yeah, what does that actually look like?<br /> <br /> *Ask me about Beast and Family Kinship sometime, only don't, because I'll cry.<br /> *Which is now World Soul/Mother's Land/Anima Mundi Goetia laquered up in a lot of Temenotic coping shit, but whatever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-13T19:10:41-07:00","id":1508313,"title":"","content":"Hmm. You know, I wasn\u2019t sold on Kinship being the \u2018Beast Integrity\u2019 trait/feature, but comparing it to Deviant\u2019s Touchstones make it understandable. Not completely, but it\u2019s getting there.<br /> <br /> Maybe Kinship \u2018Touchstones\u2019 are divided into two types like Deviant\u2019s is; the fearful, and the feared. Humans can be either, though I imagine most Beasts would start off perceiving Human Kinship as the former only.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t recall if Deviant\u2019s Touchstones had any mechanical oomph outside of being just there for the Remade to hate/love over, but if Beast\u2019s would-be equivalent would have some, (using the above dichotomy) the fearful could have something to do with finding Chambers and building Lairs, while the feared could have something to do with feeding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-13T20:10:52-07:00","id":1508322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1507340-neither-left-behind-nor-forgotten-what-do-you-want-from-kinship?p=1508313#post1508313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don\u2019t recall if Deviant\u2019s Touchstones had any mechanical oomph outside of being just there for the Remade to hate/love over,</div> </div> </div> </div>They are the main way to heal Instability, so kinda important if you don\u2019t want to be a pile of limbs and ooze.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-13T20:30:02-07:00","id":1508324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1507340-neither-left-behind-nor-forgotten-what-do-you-want-from-kinship?p=1508313#post1508313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. You know, I wasn\u2019t sold on Kinship being the \u2018Beast Integrity\u2019 trait/feature, but comparing it to Deviant\u2019s Touchstones make it understandable. Not completely, but it\u2019s getting there.<br /> <br /> Maybe Kinship \u2018Touchstones\u2019 are divided into two types like Deviant\u2019s is; the fearful, and the feared. Humans can be either, though I imagine most Beasts would start off perceiving Human Kinship as the former only.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t recall if Deviant\u2019s Touchstones had any mechanical oomph outside of being just there for the Remade to hate/love over, but if Beast\u2019s would-be equivalent would have some, (using the above dichotomy) the fearful could have something to do with finding Chambers and building Lairs, while the feared could have something to do with feeding.</div> </div> </div> </div>Deviant's Touchstones affect how durable their Conviction and Loyalty are by their quantity (which in turn affects those Touchstones' ability to influence them and their Stubborn Resolve's ability to resist being made to stop pursuing the drives of their Conviction and Loyalty), provide their main work-around for &quot;killing someone in a fight where your intention didn't include causing harm costs you Willpower,&quot; and several higher-Magnitude Scars (e.g. Frozen Heart, Hallucinations, Murderous Urge, Paranoia, Trusting) mess with the way they work or rely on them for exceptions.<br /> <br /> I feel it's worth sharing that I also briefly discussed mortal Touchstones with Arc last year, where I floated it as a category where the game currently puts blood relatives, the targets of your Horror being a recurring nightmare, your Herald, Heroes entangled with your Legend, and other such &quot;priority targets.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-13T20:50:25-07:00","id":1508326,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve always thought one of the main not really explored parts of Beast was empathy. A Beast gets it, really gets it. They know both being the monster, and being the prey. I think any Kinship must start there. And you know, people can be both too. I don\u2019t think it needs to be anywhere near Needs Must, but I think with even the basic level of Kinship should be able come to a better understanding of what the other person is about. Maybe Needs Must expands this ability to read people\u2019s past Kin. Maybe it\u2019s a much deeper and more specific read.<br /> <br /> Um, on a slightly different track, touchstones are stabilizing influences. They keep one rooted to reality. Maybe this will sound crazy, but what if Beast Chambers didn\u2019t naturally stick around? What if they required upkeep? Having someone connected to that location, and connected to a Beast through Kinship might help keep it around. And, Insatiable, right? They can steal Chambers and Lairs. (I think, still haven\u2019t bought the Night Horrors.) Having a multiple Touchstone might help keep that from happening, by stabilizing the Chambers as something that\u2019s part of the Beast, and themselves. Kinda like a sleepwalker holding a spell in Mage.<br /> <br /> So here\u2019s an another weird idea. I\u2019ve been thinking of a group of very tight knit friends who all \u201cshare\u201d the Horror. Really, only one of them is the Beast, but they all are close enough for it to work and feed through them and their actions. Might be a double edged sword, to share your heart with someone else so deeply, though. Even if they aren\u2019t the full thing, Anathema can be placed on any of them to affect the rest. Might be an idea for Max Kinship with Humans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1507340-neither-left-behind-nor-forgotten-what-do-you-want-from-kinship?p=1508311#post1508311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Ask me about Beast and Family Kinship sometime, only don't, because I'll cry.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tears are not evil. Today\u2019s Tears can water tomorrow\u2019s flowers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 04-14-2023, 12:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-13T20:59:30-07:00","id":1508327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1507340-neither-left-behind-nor-forgotten-what-do-you-want-from-kinship?p=1508326#post1508326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tears are not evil. Today\u2019s Tears can water tomorrow\u2019s flowers.</div> </div> </div> </div>The temptation to turn this into a parody of anti-Beast screeds is strong.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1507340-neither-left-behind-nor-forgotten-what-do-you-want-from-kinship?p=1508324#post1508324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel it's worth sharing that I also briefly discussed mortal Touchstones with Arc last year, where I floated it as a category where the game currently puts blood relatives, the targets of your Horror being a recurring nightmare, your Herald, Heroes entangled with your Legend, and other such &quot;priority targets.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It's been a bit since I visited this angle of attack, I need to play with it a bit\u200b.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-14T08:10:12-07:00","id":1508360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1507340-neither-left-behind-nor-forgotten-what-do-you-want-from-kinship?p=1508311#post1508311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My main interest was that I was fascinated by the metaphysical position Beasts have as Temenotic Goetia** meaning that they were a multitudinous entity-or, more accurately, they were a part of a whole lot of other people who <i>had</i> those fears and hungers. That was a angle Beast never really tackled or took advantage. There were a lot of other benefits to Human Kinship, in theory-Beast could directly get into how all fiction has a level of psychological metaphor in it, it allowed us to more readily begin constructing Beast's unspoken notion that it's neck of the world has the internal worlds and external world is one as a more solid and open thing, and it allowed people to more readily understanding Beasts as psychological actors (if they chose to be) and how that ties into their role of mythmakers and legend-takers-but mostly it was a chance to get <i>weird</i> and I like <i>weird</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see this as a reminder that Beast needs the Lore System. Feedback loops describing how events, mental states of those involved, public perception of those events and consequent Astral changes all affect each other, and how the Begotten hold an unique position in that system. Perhaps, working on that would reveal a flavorful niche for Human Kinships? I assume many other subsystems could shift their themes if meant to feed into that ruleset.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1507340-neither-left-behind-nor-forgotten-what-do-you-want-from-kinship?p=1508311#post1508311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, it had to be distinctive from other Kinship, and that became doubly true when I grokked onto Kinship being akin to Deviant's Touchstone &quot;Integrity&quot; System. That there was a power in not really being able to understand themselves by direct comparison to humanity but in how the monsters they related to related to humanity, and how that reflected back on that was a bonus way to think about it and cut a line between the two. Plus my argument about the interesting metaphysical difference has it's clear difference-Beasts are Astral Symbols of the idea of monster and feel kinship to those who arguably bear the same semiotic device, but with humans they get more into the meaning and reason behind the creation of those symbols in the first place.<br /> <br /> (I don't have any place to put this, so I'll just take this interrim to mention I don't think we need really do anything for understanding Kinship and what allows for it-Beasts have a different relationship with humanity than with monsters, and thus it follows, and what is and is not Kin is pretty clear cut, my main evidence for that being that most people were questioning if Deviants were Kin while my handful of remaining questions of what counts include those with the Cursed Merit and the question of if the Ascending Ones' alchemy actually counts.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Your preference seems to be to reinforce the metaphysical lines between Humans and Monsters, whereas mine was to blur them. Still, I'm intrigued by your approach, as described here. I do want to poke at it, though. How would the Astral react to wide swaths of the human population othering and dehumanizing an ethnicity or class of their choice? If a Human family deems a child with birth defects a monster, and has a majority of their community agreeing, what is the closest type of Kin the child could classify as?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1507340-neither-left-behind-nor-forgotten-what-do-you-want-from-kinship?p=1508311#post1508311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll lay out the three particular ideas I had, but admittedly the big thing is that while the whole idea feels meaningful and weighty, that it has bearing that could be of real aid to Beast, it's hard to actually get down into what it should do.<br /> <br /> 1) Touchstone. Even with the comprehension about Kinship and it's Integrity role, pretty much everyone I know has said that some kind of Touchstone would be a good idea-and I agree, but I do't know <i>why,</i> mostly because I can't really fathom what it would <i>do</i>. Asides from laying a fat thumb of the scales for Idea 5 from normal Kinship in favor of being associated with human inclined entitites, I'm not quite sure what a Beast should get out of it, or what a touchstone might get in kind.</div> </div> </div> </div>A first thing that comes to mind: You mentioned that you see Beast as a game of managing your brand, and I like that approach. Could Touchstones help you stay grounded, so you know which parts of your reputation overlap with your true identity, and which could break you if you tried to live up to them? I feel that Anathema could be relevant, somehow.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-16T11:07:36-07:00","id":1508543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1507340-neither-left-behind-nor-forgotten-what-do-you-want-from-kinship?p=1508360#post1508360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your preference seems to be to reinforce the metaphysical lines between Humans and Monsters, whereas mine was to blur them. Still, I'm intrigued by your approach, as described here. I do want to poke at it, though. How would the Astral react to wide swaths of the human population othering and dehumanizing an ethnicity or class of their choice? If a Human family deems a child with birth defects a monster, and has a majority of their community agreeing, what is the closest type of Kin the child could classify as?</div> </div> </div> </div>Usually my preferences hew towards greater mystery and complexity, but in this case, there's a few reasons I don't swing that way.<br /> <br /> 1) From a purely practical standpoint, the bookkeeping of Kinship can be a pain in the ass if Beast's have to go and ask &quot;Do they count as Kin so I can use a major portion of my tool kit?&quot; Keeping it simple, maybe even making it simpler, let's the game just play.<br /> <br /> 2) Given the role of semiotics in Beast, the icon of monster is inclined to have more housed in it than not, and it would become increasingly incoherent to create more variation on what does and does not count based on the metaphysic Kinship works from.<br /> <br /> 3) Also, from a thematic point, the world of Chronicles is not pre-disposed to lean towards subjective influence-the world has more objective forms and powers and nature, and public perception only rarely has affect. Now Beast is a good place to play around with that, because as you mention in a bit, Beast is a game of managing your brand-but there's a floor to how much I'd go with that.<br /> <br /> 4) On a human care perspective that relates to the humanism of the series, I'm not hyper comfortable with the metaphysical label of monster applying to people, particularly the disadvantaged of our world, in the same certifiable way one actually applies it to the actual monsters in the series. I think there's a line between a Namtaru who toys with the fear of the scarred and disabled and people who are just scarred or disabled that crossing would only do bad things for. The metaphorical and supernatural is one thing, but the instant we say &quot;You are monster because people think you are&quot; in world with actual monsters gets...again, it gets uncomfortable.<br /> <br /> I'd rather keep the qualifications of Kin simple and finite for entry. In terms of expanding it, I'd rather make it deeper and more relationship work rather than murkier, harder to work with, and somewhat unfortunate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A first thing that comes to mind: You mentioned that you see Beast as a game of managing your brand, and I like that approach. Could Touchstones help you stay grounded, so you know which parts of your reputation overlap with your true identity, and which could break you if you tried to live up to them? I feel that Anathema could be relevant, somehow.\u200b </div> </div> </div>An interesting notion that leans also into Satchel's suggestion, but I run into the issue of &quot;What does that look like?&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-16T11:47:53-07:00","id":1508546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1507340-neither-left-behind-nor-forgotten-what-do-you-want-from-kinship?p=1508543#post1508543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An interesting notion that leans also into Satchel's suggestion, but I run into the issue of &quot;What does that look like?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Could be that a brand is inherently unstable, surging past one\u2019s reach, or waning down to embers. Without proper management, a Beast could be subject to the telephone game, or misunderstanding, and have parts of their brand warp semi-permanently. One way to manage that is having a connection with someone who truly gets the real you\u2026and the brand, and working against the natural ebb and flow of myth. Uhh, I guess it\u2019s kinda like the \u201cwords of the author\u201d trope if instead it came from friends who hung around the author when they were writing. Provides clarity and something like stability, but people might reject their words about what a story meant.<br /> <br /> Mechanically, I guess I would roll\u2026Lair every time a Beast does something that would affect the brand, and over a period of time of like a month or so, to see how many sub myths popped up and how far the brand has drifted, with touchstones acting as a penalty to the roll. If they succeed at it, something not minor, but fixable happens, like a chamber needing repair. If they get an exceptional, then they get an Anathema that makes \u201csense\u201d for their archetype of Horror.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-16T12:10:01-07:00","id":1508549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1507340-neither-left-behind-nor-forgotten-what-do-you-want-from-kinship?p=1508360#post1508360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would the Astral react to wide swaths of the human population othering and dehumanizing an ethnicity or class of their choice? If a Human family deems a child with birth defects a monster, and has a majority of their community agreeing, what is the closest type of Kin the child could classify as?\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I had a thought on this on the way to work, so:<br /> <br /> As I mentioned, I'm not comfortable with passively allowing humanity's beliefs to change a person's metaphysical mark-just because humanity believes something doesn't make them right-but there is something in the angle of imposition that's a big deal of Heroes that I can get behind. Passively believing someone is a monster won't do it, but I think when we get around to hammering out how people can manipulate the Dreaming, both deliberately and accidentally, as well as how the Dreaming can intrude as a result of actions, the &quot;Force you to be Kin&quot; thing can be viable. But again, it can't just be passive belief, there has to be something where someone(s) take that passive belief and use it like a hammer or a spear. And of course, I'm also open to Heroes having the ability to, at cost, brand someone as a monster with their metaphysical authority (Probably 3 Satiety).<br /> <br /> Asides from coming off as &quot;Kin, but it feels wrong&quot; for Beasts, it also creates some fun where there's an ongoing risk that such shit can result in a person being a beacon for supernatural forces, and an ongoing risk that someone <i>becomes</i> a monster as a result. And that fits in with one of the other things I want to see going forward, being the involvement of Astral Gods and mechanics for them making monsters out of people-having humanity en masse be able to do similar <i>is</i> appealing.<br /> <br /> I'll mull on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-16T13:15:49-07:00","id":1508555,"title":"","content":"Also, the Lore system really needs a better name. Wonder if I can get away with a demon, demon, or demon invocation and call it Legacy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-16T13:33:02-07:00","id":1508557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1507340-neither-left-behind-nor-forgotten-what-do-you-want-from-kinship?p=1508555#post1508555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, the Lore system really needs a better name. Wonder if I can get away with a demon, demon, or demon invocation and call it Legacy.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026maybe. Not really sure that fits. I like Morals, but it doesn\u2019t have the L. I wish I had good word for the stuff that grounds a story to reality enough for us to visualize it. You know, the thing that breaks when characters act irrationally and maintains the suspension of disbelief.<br /> <br /> Edit: maybe Theme?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 04-16-2023, 04:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-16T13:54:26-07:00","id":1508560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1507340-neither-left-behind-nor-forgotten-what-do-you-want-from-kinship?p=1508557#post1508557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026maybe. Not really sure that fits. I like Morals, but it doesn\u2019t have the L. I wish I had good word for the stuff that grounds a story to reality enough for us to visualize it. You the thing that breaks when characters act irrationally and maintains the suspension of disbelief.<br /> <br /> Edit: maybe Theme?</div> </div> </div> </div>Theme's a little bland, and not really on the point of the system, where taking lessons from a Beast's myth as a way to act and be empowers people. Legacy, at least, ties into reputation as a thing that people act on and in aspiration of. Batman begets Batmen and such.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-16T15:04:06-07:00","id":1508568,"title":"","content":"The closest word in current existence that I could find is Mimesis, where Art imitates Life. Given that\u2019s a philosophical concept, they do have a word for the inverted concept of Life imitating Art: Anti-Mimesis. Doesn\u2019t exactly roll off the tongue. Other concepts kinda related are Synchronicity, and Syzygy. But I don\u2019t know if those are any better. All of them sound like what a Mage would term the concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-16T15:09:50-07:00","id":1508570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1507340-neither-left-behind-nor-forgotten-what-do-you-want-from-kinship?p=1508555#post1508555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, the Lore system really needs a better name. Wonder if I can get away with a demon, demon, or demon invocation and call it Legacy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Learning?<br /> <br /> Maybe the whole talk about \u2018Beasts teaching lessons\u2019 is in-universe moral myopia on the Begotten\u2019s side; what\u2019s really happening is that the people are taking their own slices off the whole piece, where Beasts are only setting up the general direction.<br /> <br /> E.g. When a Nemesis physically beats up a petty tyrant (abusive boss, abusive parent, abusive cop, etc.) some people get the Lesson that tyrants aren\u2019t worth listening to, but some people get the lesson that physical strength is what you really need to protect yourself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-16T15:13:12-07:00","id":1508571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1507340-neither-left-behind-nor-forgotten-what-do-you-want-from-kinship?p=1508570#post1508570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Learning?<br /> <br /> Maybe the whole talk about \u2018Beasts teaching lessons\u2019 is in-universe moral myopia on the Begotten\u2019s side; what\u2019s really happening is that the people are taking their own slices off the whole piece, where Beasts are only setting up the general direction.<br /> <br /> E.g. When a Nemesis physically beats up a petty tyrant (abusive boss, abusive parent, abusive cop, etc.) some people get the Lesson that tyrants aren\u2019t worth listening to, but some people get the lesson that physical strength is what you really need to protect yourself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, I want to move beyond lessons and into myth-making and psychodrama. Also, while I like the L-naming scheme, we might be a little too hung up on it.<br /> <br /> I like Mimesis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 04-16-2023, 06:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-16T20:10:05-07:00","id":1508599,"title":"","content":"There <i>is </i>a low-hanging fruit in the L-scheme. I'd say it's License.<br /> <br /> All myths are examples and justifications - something has happened before, and it's way less scary to use what you've been told happened in the past as a yardstick to guide your choices than to face the Great Wide Unknown. Growing your Lair means you accept to become that example, that precedent.<br /> <br /> That can be through your Legend, as in the case above of a Nemesis toppling a tyrant boss: you gave his employees the proof that a) the boss himself is fallible, and b) all seats of authority might be similarly flawed. It's not a moral lesson, not a ruling: it's not forcing, or even directly <i>allowing </i>them to take action. But... there's something there, something they didn't do because<i> &quot;</i><i>nobody does that</i><i>&quot;</i>, or &quot;<i>nobody normal would do that</i><i>&quot;</i>, or <i>&quot;nobody would back me up if I did that&quot;</i>, and now there's a voice in the back of their head saying &quot;<i>welp, seems like somebody just done did that, and who was there to stop them?&quot;</i><br /> <br /> But that could also be through your Life: not taking the boss' shit and quitting, or cooperating with him to find his good side. Proving that sometimes, in the situations when human society <i>expects </i>and valorizes behaving like an Apex Predator, it's okay (and even more rebellious) to say <i>&quot;screw that, screw that game, I'm not playing it&quot;</i>.<br /> <br /> And this kind of breakthroughs obviously consolidate your role as a Beast. The humans or kin that imitate realize they <i>can, </i>like you, exert a level of agency that makes them dangerous. And that gives them moral responsibility, whatever they end up doing with it. It pairs up well with the core themes of the homebrew Lineages write-ups. You're afraid, and your fears are - at least partially - justified, and there's no guidebook in the world that can teach you the perfect way to face them because there's no perfect. And That's Okay.<br /> <br /> But obviously, that is also why Heroes hunt you down. This dangerous freedom and chaos you bring, predicated on the idea that we should all behave as if we were still naked and afraid in the wild, despite the clothes and the street lights and the concrete ? That's counter to all values. Even the not-Zealot Heroes who are not completely convinced <i>their </i>way is the natural right way worry about what happens if your example spreads beyond you, emboldens mortals or supernatural creatures to become accepting of their monstrosity. The underlings of the boss you've beat might take it as License to become bullies of their own. Each of your accomplishments can be construed into a License to put you down, before the spread of your ideas damage society beyond repair.<br /> <br /> And the Insatiable whittling them down ? Well, as the Titans of this dark-Scion, they're Nature, cold uncaring alien nature. The very hard-to-argue-against notion that for the handful of individuals for which your example matters, there's a vastly wider world who doesn't give a single care.<br /> <br /> I can understand if the word is too administrative in English to make it work as IG lingo. In French, <i>licence </i>is often used in poetry used when an author or creator takes a departure from the usual rules (e.g. spelling) when it serves their artwork better - that probably helps in making it so compelling to me.<br /> <br /> If we privilege the aspect of mythology and recurrence, I'd say Leitmotiv. If we drop the L-scheme, I would probably call it a Beast's Wake. Because it wakes up people in their wake, obviously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11431-adrasalieth","user":"Adrasalieth","date":". 04-17-2023, 12:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11431-adrasalieth","name":"Adrasalieth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-16T20:14:57-07:00","id":1508600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1507340-neither-left-behind-nor-forgotten-what-do-you-want-from-kinship?p=1508549#post1508549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I mentioned, I'm not comfortable with passively allowing humanity's beliefs to change a person's metaphysical mark-just because humanity believes something doesn't make them right-but there is something in the angle of imposition that's a big deal of Heroes that I can get behind. Passively believing someone is a monster won't do it, but I think when we get around to hammering out how people can manipulate the Dreaming, both deliberately and accidentally, as well as how the Dreaming can intrude as a result of actions, the &quot;Force you to be Kin&quot; thing can be viable. But again, it can't just be passive belief, there has to be something where someone(s) take that passive belief and use it like a hammer or a spear. And of course, I'm also open to Heroes having the ability to, at cost, brand someone as a monster with their metaphysical authority (Probably 3 Satiety).<br /> <br /> Asides from coming off as &quot;Kin, but it feels wrong&quot; for Beasts, it also creates some fun where there's an ongoing risk that such shit can result in a person being a beacon for supernatural forces, and an ongoing risk that someone <i>becomes</i> a monster as a result. And that fits in with one of the other things I want to see going forward, being the involvement of Astral Gods and mechanics for them making monsters out of people-having humanity en masse be able to do similar <i>is</i> appealing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I'm not too into the idea of Beast presenting a mode by which the Bright Dream can explicitly turn people into monsters without leveraging Primordial power to do so, for reasons complementary to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1422382-legend-embellishment-and-the-siege-of-the-bright-dream-assorted-brainstorming?p=1492195#post1492195\">stuff I've gone over about Heroes</a> \u2014 the Temenos mostly doesn't work along that axis of supernatural power, and in my view the avenues where it does should either produce results analogous to the circumstances that produce Beasts (whether normal specimens or the products of Inheritances) or not be explicitly tied to that process at all a la &quot;did rumors turn this guy into a monster or predict something that was going to happen anyway?&quot; ambiguity that can feed into the splat's grappling with fatalism and sort of feels Persona-adjacent.<br /> <br /> The way Begotten's sense for the supernatural works means that they'll be able to tell if they're one of their fellow Children (optimally-stabilized or otherwise), and if they're not then they'll be able to identify another specimen of that type of monstrosity if it recurs, but the Bright Dream's responsibility for monsters in the metaphysics as it stands is most analogous to the reveal about why a given modern Persona game's ultimate antagonist showed up, i.e. collective humanity gave a demon a name to answer to and it came when they called for it.<br /> <br /> Some of this does kind of run afoul of Werewolf's issues with presenting mortals as a danger before bringing in Shadow occultists and the like, in that it necessarily makes the bulk of their danger a passive and unknowing one, but it's worth remembering that most of the Temenos's established ability to directly mess with individual people relies on those people being famous and possessed by the avatars of their fame. I personally wouldn't connect the Bright Dream to deliberately establishing any degree of monstrosity greater than that presented by gaining Supernatural Merits \u2014 if it out-monsters a Herald, it should probably be a Beast (with or without an Inheritance modifying the final outcome, because in my view that's half the point of those Inheritances), an Insatiable, or something else that a Dreamer could nevertheless see coming through the Dark Dream's nightmare filter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-17T21:59:39-07:00","id":1508710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1507340-neither-left-behind-nor-forgotten-what-do-you-want-from-kinship?p=1508549#post1508549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I had a thought on this on the way to work, so:<br /> <br /> As I mentioned, I'm not comfortable with passively allowing humanity's beliefs to change a person's metaphysical mark-just because humanity believes something doesn't make them right-but there is something in the angle of imposition that's a big deal of Heroes that I can get behind. Passively believing someone is a monster won't do it, but I think when we get around to hammering out how people can manipulate the Dreaming, both deliberately and accidentally, as well as how the Dreaming can intrude as a result of actions, the &quot;Force you to be Kin&quot; thing can be viable. But again, it can't just be passive belief, there has to be something where someone(s) take that passive belief and use it like a hammer or a spear. And of course, I'm also open to Heroes having the ability to, at cost, brand someone as a monster with their metaphysical authority (Probably 3 Satiety).<br /> <br /> Asides from coming off as &quot;Kin, but it feels wrong&quot; for Beasts, it also creates some fun where there's an ongoing risk that such shit can result in a person being a beacon for supernatural forces, and an ongoing risk that someone <i>becomes</i> a monster as a result. And that fits in with one of the other things I want to see going forward, being the involvement of Astral Gods and mechanics for them making monsters out of people-having humanity en masse be able to do similar <i>is</i> appealing.<br /> <br /> I'll mull on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am a bit late to this and it's been a long while since I last posted here, but reading this up reminds me how Scion 2e solved this in regards to gods and belief, in which in order for it to work said god must be enforcing the idea.<br /> <br /> An example I can give is if everyone for some reason suddenly believed Thor is a Healer.... not only would that not work but Thor would be confused and fate/world would also be confused and try and reapply Thor's history back in place over whatever's trying to make everyone think Thor is a healer, in order for that change to apply Thor themselves must enforce that belief (I.E heal people, fix communities etc.) in order for that to stick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T08:51:15-07:00","id":1508752,"title":"","content":"Saw this and decided to take a look, then saw the current discussion and it's all pretty much going over my head, so I'll stick to the original question and go for more stuff in the mechanics, Kinship was basically barely there on the Player's Guide, I mean there are about two lines worth of text about how to make your own, less powerful than atavism seems the most of what I can remember from what the book says, would have loved to see some expanded guidelines to come up with your own stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24813-aeveth","name":"Aeveth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T15:00:51-07:00","id":1508928,"title":"","content":"I'll try to go through your arguments one by one, not because I'm confident in my position, but because I have little to offer if I don't commit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1507340-neither-left-behind-nor-forgotten-what-do-you-want-from-kinship?p=1508543#post1508543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) From a purely practical standpoint, the bookkeeping of Kinship can be a pain in the ass if Beast's have to go and ask &quot;Do they count as Kin so I can use a major portion of my tool kit?&quot; Keeping it simple, maybe even making it simpler, let's the game just play.<br /> <br /> 2) Given the role of semiotics in Beast, the icon of monster is inclined to have more housed in it than not, and it would become increasingly incoherent to create more variation on what does and does not count based on the metaphysic Kinship works from.</div> </div> </div> </div>If anything, letting Humans be Kin would simplify the matter. You don't need to figure out which edge case gets Kinship benefits and which one doesn't. If that seems like too much, you've already suggested Kinship as a tiered Condition - ordinary Humans (and animals) could be simply confined to lower levels, and only literal Monsters could get the whole metaphysical oomph.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1507340-neither-left-behind-nor-forgotten-what-do-you-want-from-kinship?p=1508543#post1508543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) Also, from a thematic point, the world of Chronicles is not pre-disposed to lean towards subjective influence-the world has more objective forms and powers and nature, and public perception only rarely has affect. Now Beast is a good place to play around with that, because as you mention in a bit, Beast is a game of managing your brand-but there's a floor to how much I'd go with that.<br /> <br /> 4) On a human care perspective that relates to the humanism of the series, I'm not hyper comfortable with the metaphysical label of monster applying to people, particularly the disadvantaged of our world, in the same certifiable way one actually applies it to the actual monsters in the series. I think there's a line between a Namtaru who toys with the fear of the scarred and disabled and people who are just scarred or disabled that crossing would only do bad things for. The metaphorical and supernatural is one thing, but the instant we say &quot;You are monster because people think you are&quot; in world with actual monsters gets...again, it gets uncomfortable.<br /> <br /> I'd rather keep the qualifications of Kin simple and finite for entry. In terms of expanding it, I'd rather make it deeper and more relationship work rather than murkier, harder to work with, and somewhat unfortunate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sensitive writing is the most important objection you raised. Especially for a gameline which borked that before. Having said that, I think the right framing could make this work. I'll start with a lesser point:<br /> <br /> The Astral contains all concepts shared between multiple people, therefore it must contain a realm that equates &quot;undesireables&quot; with monsters. The Bright Dream would contain conscious narratives and excuses, but The Primordial Dream would connect to instincts and gut reactions from which conscious responses flow. That doesn't make such demonisation morally of factually correct. It would just mean that sheer pressure of human perception would push victims into Beasts' metaphysical backyard.<br /> <br /> My major point: Let's depict it as profoundly messed up. An average Beast would resonate both with literal (likely harmful) Monsters, and Humans who experienced some of the worst Humanity had to offer. This has the added benefit of having the game not <i>needing</i> other monsters to work - the human drama offers plenty material already (especially for players who do want to tackle heavy subjects in a safe environment). How the Begotten respond to that situation would tell a lot about their character. Do they accept them as Family in an us-versus-the-world mindset (this would be a mixed blessing at best, coming from living Nightmares)? Do they consider this state a malfunction of society, requiring some strategically deployed terror to make the community rethink its priorities? Do they consider them a sacrifice by Humanity to the Mother (for her hunger or her love). A potential book could include a Human NPC in just such a situation to drive the point home, that this is not a good situation to be in.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1507340-neither-left-behind-nor-forgotten-what-do-you-want-from-kinship?p=1508543#post1508543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An interesting notion that leans also into Satchel's suggestion, but I run into the issue of &quot;What does that look like?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm in the same camp as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/\">TempleBuilder</a> . In fact, I once had a silly idea of a character's Horror becoming such a prominent urban legend, it started being used as a Cereal mascot without the Beast's consent. A cutesy version begun entrenching itself in the Dream and overwriting the legendry. Would a Beast choose violence to get her reputation on the right track, or use that as a springboard to a constricted but wide infamy. Another bit of brand management would be that sometimes, needs of the brand and needs of the individual are at odds. Perhaps you worked hard to be seen as a fair but firmly cruel tempter, but the Hero endangering your family is not interested in playing along. He needs to die ASAP, but the witnesses and, God forbid, the rumour mill can't connect you to his death, or your brand will shift in unpredictable directions.<br /> <br /> I don't know how to approach this mechanically. Perhaps Scion has a useful mechanic that could be repurposed (I don't have the game)? Perhaps reusing Deviant's Conspiracy actions to govern reputations? Lair Chambers would be not just useful infrastructure, but could hold and anchor fragments of reputation: The Namtaru wants reduce opiates addiction in the community. She befouls the house of an unscrupulous doctor, forms a Chamber there and writes &quot;The Slug Swarm befouls the homes of corrupt medics (+2 to relevant dice rolls within the Hive)&quot; into the Primordial Dream. She must now fight to stay on top of that narrative - the doctor must struggle in vain to clean up his house, but can't rethink is life, because he would no longer be corrupt.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T17:16:50-07:00","id":1508942,"title":"","content":"Seems weird to assign dot ratings or equivalent to each instance of Family Ties, and probably won't yield much to justify the extra book-keeping. I think that Family Ties should remain a mostly narrative consideration, with particulars like &quot;how much do you care about this relationship?&quot; and &quot;are you rivals or friends?&quot; being handled via roleplay. If you want some kind of &quot;dot rating&quot; for Family Ties to determine how easy it is to develop corresponding Kinship Merits, I'm pretty sure making it more of a two-way mechanic would be sufficient. The Kin gets Beats for neglecting other aspects of their lives to help the Beast, and in turn the Beast gets Beats for enabling the more monstrous side of the Kin in one way or another.<br /> <br /> If your Beast spends more time on maintaining and expanding this two-way dynamic, he gets more Beats and thus can afford higher-rated Kinship Merits more quickly. THAT right there is you effective &quot;dot rating&quot; associated with Family Ties, IMO. Besides, assigning objective values of psycho-spiritual importance to a list of Kin seems weird, and might also result in arguments with the ST about whether or not Family Ties Level 3 has been arbitrarily reached, or if you are still at Family Ties Level 1 because the ST doesn't agree that your interactions with the Kin were meaningful enough. How many people IRL consciously give grades to their relationships and make quantitative comparisons between those grades?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T17:18:47-07:00","id":1508943,"title":"","content":"\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1507340-neither-left-behind-nor-forgotten-what-do-you-want-from-kinship?p=1508928#post1508928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Astral contains all concepts shared between multiple people, therefore it must contain a realm that equates &quot;undesireables&quot; with monsters. The Bright Dream would contain conscious narratives and excuses, but The Primordial Dream would connect to instincts and gut reactions from which conscious responses flow. That doesn't make such demonisation morally of factually correct. It would just mean that sheer pressure of human perception would push victims into Beasts' metaphysical backyard.</div> </div> </div> </div> I\u2019d just like to add on to this, in that every human being ever to be born will have some traits considered objectionable by the greater whole of humanity. Maybe even including themselves. Beasts roughly correspond to the Id, the shadow self. Kinship with a Beast I think would be built on that part, both the acceptance of of the Shadow, and that Humanity at large believes a part of them to be Monstrous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T17:24:48-07:00","id":1508945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1507340-neither-left-behind-nor-forgotten-what-do-you-want-from-kinship?p=1508942#post1508942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seems weird to assign dot ratings or equivalent to each instance of Family Ties, and probably won't yield much to justify the extra book-keeping. I think that Family Ties should remain a mostly narrative consideration, with particulars like &quot;how much do you care about this relationship?&quot; and &quot;are you rivals or friends?&quot; being handled via roleplay. If you want some kind of &quot;dot rating&quot; for Family Ties to determine how easy it is to develop corresponding Kinship Merits, I'm pretty sure making it more of a two-way mechanic would be sufficient. The Kin gets Beats for neglecting other aspects of their lives to help the Beast, and in turn the Beast gets Beats for enabling the more monstrous side of the Kin in one way or another.<br /> <br /> If your Beast spends more time on maintaining and expanding this two-way dynamic, he gets more Beats and thus can afford higher-rated Kinship Merits more quickly. THAT right there is you effective &quot;dot rating&quot; associated with Family Ties, IMO. Besides, assigning objective values of psycho-spiritual importance to a list of Kin seems weird, and might also result in arguments with the ST about whether or not Family Ties Level 3 has been arbitrarily reached, or if you are still at Family Ties Level 1 because the ST doesn't agree that your interactions with the Kin were meaningful enough. How many people IRL consciously give grades to their relationships and make quantitative comparisons between those grades?</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh\u2026I think people do just that. I think it goes unknown &gt; acquaintance/coworker &gt; friend &gt; best friend &gt; life partner<br /> Whether a relationship is romantic might be another axis people use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 04-19-2023, 08:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T18:11:48-07:00","id":1508957,"title":"","content":"So, I was chatting with Gibbering through private messages about whether humans actually rank relationships, (I was of the opinion they do), and it was brought up that the Chronicles System does in fact do this in several places, namely certain merits, and in mage, sympathetic connections. Would sympathetic connections be a good place to model different levels of Kinship? Might help with clarity of the definition and differentiation of certain ranks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T18:15:37-07:00","id":1508959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1507340-neither-left-behind-nor-forgotten-what-do-you-want-from-kinship?p=1508928#post1508928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sensitive writing is the most important objection you raised. Especially for a gameline which borked that before. Having said that, I think the right framing could make this work.</div> </div> </div> </div>On this particular vein, my biggest problem is judging the line where it crosses...<br /> <br /> Actually, for my articulation, i'm going to start at the opposite end of the spectrum. There's this idea in games design and criticism where it doesn't matter if a game comments negatively on a thing if the game allows you do the thing anyways, even if it somehow renders playing onward in a negative way-a good short way to explain it is &quot;It doesn't matter if you lose points for killing hookers in your game, the game still allows you to kill hookers and therefore contributes to the overarching problem of accepting violence against hookers as normal.&quot; It doesn't matter if the content is condemned on the other side of the action-if there is content beyond the action, then it is an accepted part of the game.<br /> <br /> Now, TTRPG's have a weird relationship to this, and games that deal with transgressive ideas and roleplay get even weirder, and Beast as a game that has Transgression as a major element of it's DNA is going to be a place that requires maturity about it. As a general rule, I lean into Beast's relationship to transgression as a positive for a mature roleplaying game expected for a mature roleplaying group, which is a flirtation with danger, but arguably not particularly above any of the other game lines.<br /> <br /> On this point though, I <i>worry</i>. It's a situation where I have to ask myself &quot;Does it matter if I make it clear that this is a kind of really fucked up thing to do, (particularly by tying it into the most assholish element about Heroes as my beginning baseline, as I followed up on), if at the end of the day I still put in content that effectively lets someone create scenarios where people, particularly the disadvantaged in society, are read as monsters in a world with actual monsters?&quot;<br /> <br /> There's a lot of things I'm willing to flirt with on Beast, and I get the appeal of this sort of mechanic, but on the other hand, whenever I really think about it, I keep arriving at the only correct thing to do is to not suggest content on the other side of that action.<br /> <br /> That's not a hard no, just-I really want to think about this, even longer than I already have, and this has come up a few times already.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T18:19:34-07:00","id":1508960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1507340-neither-left-behind-nor-forgotten-what-do-you-want-from-kinship?p=1508957#post1508957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I was chatting with Gibbering through private messages about whether humans actually rank relationships, (I was of the opinion they do), and it was brought up that the Chronicles System does in fact do this in several places, namely certain merits, and in mage, sympathetic connections. Would sympathetic connections be a good place to model different levels of Kinship? Might help with clarity of the definition and differentiation of certain ranks.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, it's good precedent, but for that aspect of it all, precedent is not direly important.<br /> <br /> Also, arguably any scaling Social merit portrays the same. Also, the Impression rating in Social Maneveuring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T18:53:19-07:00","id":1508965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1507340-neither-left-behind-nor-forgotten-what-do-you-want-from-kinship?p=1508959#post1508959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not a hard no, just-I really want to think about this, even longer than I already have, and this has come up a few times already.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think anyone has an answer for you, Arcane. That's something for you to decide, and nobody can make that decision for you. Everyone has different standards and different things they find upsetting and unforgivable.<br /> <br /> If I may suggest something, though. Talk to people about it. Ask, hey, is this too far for a game, is it too much for art to explore? And know that they have their biases, and their quirks and no single answer is the whole picture. Not theirs, not yours. But in the end, you are the one making the call. Make it one you can live with, both the good and the bad.<br /> <br /> I think any topic, no matter how heartbreaking, or vile can be discussed in a respectful and kind manner. Some topics need to be addressed. Not everyone feels the same way, they would rather bury parts of Human nature they don't like. Which is better? I cannot say.<br /> <br /> Changeling covers Trauma in all its forms, through the lens of a game. And it is well beloved. It provokes thoughts that need to be raised and makes us question our lives, and what they mean. Do you think that Beast can cover Monstrosity in the same way? I do. It's not going to be easy, and there are so many point of failure that will need to be overcome, but I think Beast can the greatest of all the gamelines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 04-19-2023, 09:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T18:55:07-07:00","id":1508966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1507340-neither-left-behind-nor-forgotten-what-do-you-want-from-kinship?p=1508965#post1508965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think anyone has an answer for you, Arcane. That's something for you to decide, and nobody can make that decision for you. Everyone has different standards and different things they find upsetting and unforgivable.<br /> <br /> If I may suggest something, though. Talk to people about it. Ask, hey, is this too far for a game, is it too much for art to explore? And know that they have their biases, and their quirks and no single answer is the whole picture. Not theirs, not yours. But in the end, you are the one making the call. Make it one you can live with.<br /> <br /> I think any topic, no matter how heartbreaking, or vile can be discussed in a respectful and kind manner. Some topics need to be addressed. Not everyone feels the same way, they would rather bury parts of Human nature they don't like. Which is better? I cannot say.<br /> <br /> Changeling covers Trauma in all its forms, through the lens of a game. And it is well beloved. It provokes thoughts that need to be raised and makes us question our lives, and what they mean. Do you think that Beast can cover Monstrosity in the same way? I do. It's not going to be easy, and there are so many point of failure that will need to be overcome, but I think Beast can the greatest of all the gamelines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Way ahead of you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T19:24:00-07:00","id":1508971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1507340-neither-left-behind-nor-forgotten-what-do-you-want-from-kinship?p=1508928#post1508928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Astral contains all concepts shared between multiple people, therefore it must contain a realm that equates &quot;undesireables&quot; with monsters. The Bright Dream would contain conscious narratives and excuses, but The Primordial Dream would connect to instincts and gut reactions from which conscious responses flow. That doesn't make such demonisation morally of factually correct. It would just mean that sheer pressure of human perception would push victims into Beasts' metaphysical backyard.</div> </div> </div> </div>The connective tissue for the Primordial Dream is Lair Traits and loss of Integrity. There are Bright Realms whose Themes can match with a Beast's Lair Traits, but the Astral is <i>all</i> unconscious \u2014 the Dark Dream doesn't need to get involved at the level of conflating a class of person with a monster when it can just absorb a dream that resonates with fear of undesirables that a larval Horror can come to live in.\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1507340-neither-left-behind-nor-forgotten-what-do-you-want-from-kinship?p=1508942#post1508942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seems weird to assign dot ratings or equivalent to each instance of Family Ties, and probably won't yield much to justify the extra book-keeping. I think that Family Ties should remain a mostly narrative consideration, with particulars like &quot;how much do you care about this relationship?&quot; and &quot;are you rivals or friends?&quot; being handled via roleplay. If you want some kind of &quot;dot rating&quot; for Family Ties to determine how easy it is to develop corresponding Kinship Merits, I'm pretty sure making it more of a two-way mechanic would be sufficient. The Kin gets Beats for neglecting other aspects of their lives to help the Beast, and in turn the Beast gets Beats for enabling the more monstrous side of the Kin in one way or another.</div> </div> </div> </div>Arc is explicitly riffing on the Connection mechanic from <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/118784/Golden-Sky-Stories\" target=\"_blank\">Golden Sky Stories</a>, which serves as the source of the primary resources in that game \u2014 you get the resource that lets you use supernatural powers based on the strength of your connections to others, and you get the resource that lets you raise or lower your stats to adjust the degree to which you succeed at an action (GSS is a diceless game) based on the strength of others' connections to you, and either of these can also be used for the game's main means of not drawing attention to yourself as a magical nonhuman. (Notably, the Town the game is set in counts as a character for these purposes.)<br /> <br /> The third resource in the game is used for strengthening Connections; you can only spend that resource on characters you were in a scene with, and you can only strengthen your own Connections toward other characters (the narrator counts as a character for this purpose, which matters because getting a Connection above its third level is increasingly costly, while you can get Connections with a strength of 1 or 2 from mutually creating one with a character, though doing so will almost certainly require you to spend the stat-raising resource unless you're leaning heavily on a particular base stat, and which stat you use for the check affects the starting context of the Connection)<br /> <br /> I played a Rabbit in a game of Golden Sky Stories that Arc ran, and the default powers those get are heavily focused on Connections \u2014 every Rabbit, as a free power, gives a cost break for other characters to strengthen Connections toward them, and can spend their magical resources to bring a character they have a Connection with into the scene; two of their optional powers let them directly increase the strength of Connections other people make toward them, while a third gives them the same cost break they apply toward others for strengthening their own outgoing Connections, and a fourth lets them spend Connection-strengthening resources with characters who aren't in the scene as long as they also aren't in the scene; and the attached weaknesses that come with those particular optional powers (four of the six!) all limit your ability to act or mess with the context of your Connections in ways that aren't hard to cross-apply to habitually-Gorged Begotten who attend a lot of Family Dinners.<br /> <br /> On the other end of things, Dogs are very heavily built around the strength of their outgoing Connections \u2014 two of their universal powers scale based on how strongly you feel about the target, two of their optional powers give them a fairly strong Connection from the outset, and the attached weaknesses for two other optional powers both mess with different ends of the process for creating new Connections but explicitly doesn't apply to characters you had a Connection with in a previous story; the power attached to one of these is another one that scales based on your own feelings. I have joked that this dynamic means Dogs in GSS get infinite free magic, but it's not difficult to imagine a version of Family Ties for which this sort of thing could be used to make Mother's Kiss more effective.<br /> <br /> I can see what Arc is going for, is what I'm getting at here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}